      "text": "Ilha Grande to Paraty"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:d1bf136a4a3c936a",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "e3b83f8768c53b0593483890df6c7258d84cb3b90e0993dc9361817f31b9dbf7",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-amanda-mw6jqagc-aglbgakm8vv",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, travel to Paraty by shared boat and then by car. Check in at your hotel.\n\n\n\n\nParaty is about 125 miles from Rio and has preserved an extensive collection of 18th-century Portuguese colonial buildings. In the late 1700s, gold from Minas Gerais passed through the town on its way to the coast, where it was shipped to Portugal. The trade route later shifted towards Rio, and Paraty lost its former importance. That helped preserve the streets and buildings of the old centre with few major alterations.\n\n\n\n\nToday Paraty is a small resort town where you can explore historic streets and spend time by the sea. Low houses with colourful doors and windows line the stone-paved streets of the old centre. Beyond it are the green slopes of the Atlantic Forest and the beaches. This makes Paraty both a historic stop and a base for coastal outings."
    },
